By accessing, invoking, connecting to, or using any part of the Service, you confirm that you have read and accepted this License. If you use the Service on behalf of an organization, you represent that you have authority to bind that organization, and **“you”** includes both you and that organization.

## 1. Definitions

### 1.1 Service

The **“Service”** means the ChemBricks API, MCP server, Claude Connector, plugin, hosted prediction systems, software interfaces, documentation, databases, infrastructure, and associated services made available by ChemBricks.

### 1.2 Submitted Materials

**“Submitted Materials”** means all prompts, queries, molecular structures, chemical representations, files, datasets, parameters, instructions, metadata, experimental information, feedback, and other content submitted, transmitted, or otherwise made available through the Service.

### 1.3 Outputs

**“Outputs”** means all predictions, calculations, scores, structures, descriptors, rankings, recommendations, generated data, reports, responses, and other results produced or returned by the Service.

### 1.4 ChemBricks Technology

**“ChemBricks Technology”** means the Service and all underlying or related models, model weights, parameters, algorithms, methods, workflows, software, source code, object code, databases, training data, evaluation data, documentation, interfaces, designs, trade secrets, know-how, and intellectual property.

### 1.5 Derived Data

**“Derived Data”** means aggregated, statistical, analytical, inferred, transformed, annotated, de-identified, operational, performance, usage, telemetry, benchmarking, and other data generated from or relating to the operation or use of the Service, Submitted Materials, or Outputs.

### 1.6 Research Purpose

A **“Research Purpose”** means non-commercial scientific research, academic research, teaching, education, or internal evaluation that is not performed for commercial advantage, monetary compensation, product development, customer delivery, regulatory approval, or revenue-generating activity.

Research conducted by or on behalf of a for-profit organization is not a Research Purpose unless ChemBricks has expressly approved that use in writing.

